{number: 94}
{title: Great Is Thy Faithfulness}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Great is Thy faithfulness, [F] O God my Father,
[G7] There is no shadow of [C] turning with Thee;
Thou [C] changest not, Thy com-[F] passions they fail not;
As [D7] Thou hast been Thou for-[G7] ever wilt be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G7] Great is Thy faithfulness! [C] Great is Thy faithfulness!
[G7] Morning by morning new [C] mercies I see;
All [C] I have needed Thy [F] hand hath provided,
[C] Great is Thy faithfulness, [G7] Lord, unto [C] me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Summer and winter, and [F] springtime and harvest,
[G7] Sun, moon and stars in their [C] courses above,
Join [C] with all nature in [F] manifold witness
To [D7] Thy great faithfulness, [G7] mercy and love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Pardon for sin and a [F] peace that endureth,
[G7] Thine own dear presence to [C] cheer and to guide;
Strength [C] for today and bright [F] hope for tomorrow,
Bless-[D7] ings all mine, with ten [G7] thousand beside!
{end_of_verse}
